      "originalText": "    const filterProducts = useCallback((searchParams) => {\n        const updatedProducts = products.filter((p) => {\n            return p.title.toLowerCase().includes(searchParams.toLowerCase());\n        })\n        setFilteredProducts(updatedProducts);\n\n    }, [products]); // here is product is dependency because we are using products inside that\n                            callBack and products current value will be stored in that function (closure), so to \n                            keep this usecallback correctly using updated products data whenever its value changes\n                            so the the new reference will again store new value of products.\n\n",
